     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"The target crown:obtain is an OR of h4_3:escalate and h4_0:pivot, so both branches must be cut. Branch 1: h4_0:pivot depends only on h2_2:reach, which is an AND that needs h1_2:reach. Blocking any one of h4_0, h2_2 or h1_2 cuts this branch. Branch 2: h4_3:escalate depends only on h2_1:obtain. h2_1 is an OR of h1_0:reach and h1_2:reach, and h1_0 is fed directly by entry footholds. This branch is cut by blocking h4_3 or h2_1, or by blocking both h1_0 and h1_2. No single step lies on both branches: blocking h1_2 cuts branch 1, but h2_1 stays reachable through h1_0. So one block is not enough. Blocking {h4_0:pivot, h4_3:escalate} makes the target unreachable, so the minimum is 2.\"}"
